  "rationale": "This is an Athenian honorific decree dating to the archonship of Nicias (282/1 BC). It honors Strombichus, a soldier who originally served under Demetrius Poliorcetes but defected to the side of the Athenian people during their struggle for liberation. The text highlights his participation in the siege of the Museion hill and his continued loyalty to the democracy during subsequent warfare. The inscription is a classic example of the meritocratic language used by the restored democracy to reward those who aided in the city's freedom.",
